  "result": "I added `truncateMiddle(text, max)` in `src/core/truncate.ts` and committed it as `3518fb7`. The new tests, `tsc --noEmit` and `biome check` all pass. I didn't run the full `npm run gate` or `npm run lint`.\n\n- **Behaviour:** Text within `max` comes back unchanged. Longer text keeps both ends around a single `…`, and the result never exceeds `max` characters. When the budget is odd, the head gets the extra character, so `truncateMiddle('abcdefghij', 6)` gives `abc…ij`.\n- **Tiny limits:** `max` of 1 returns just `…`, and `max` of 0 or less returns an empty string.\n- **Existing helpers:** There was no `src/core/truncate.ts` yet, and I found nothing in `src/` to reuse, so the function is standalone. The other truncation code is one-off, such as the marker in `src/worker/cli.ts`.\n- **Tests:** `test/truncate.test.ts` is a `node:test` file covering unchanged short text, the two-ended truncation, and the tiny limits.",
